# Product photography is served from Shopify's CDN in production
# (NEXT_PUBLIC_IMG_CDN=1), where the originals are 1550x2325 vs our local
# 1200x1800 downscales. Excluding them keeps ~1.8 GB / 15,912 files out of the
# deployment, which both dodges Vercel's file-count limits and makes redeploys
# fast. The files stay in git/local for offline dev and as the fallback source.
public/bertolucci_images

# Design-time image masters. `assets/stores` holds the 1400px storefront
# originals; the deployment only ever serves the pre-generated rungs written into
# public/stores by scripts/build-store-images.py.
assets

# Never needed in a deployment
berto-lucci-final.zip
*.zip

# Local Vercel CLI state / dev OIDC token — never part of the deployment source
.vercel
.env*
